Manual review corrections:

- Exercise on points A(alpha,0,0), B(0,beta,0), C(alpha,beta,beta): the
  converted source used \overrightarrow{...} for the vector arrows while
  every other exercise in this file uses \overset{\to}{...}; normalized to
  the file's established notation. It also joined two separate equations
  (||OA+OB||=sqrt2 and ||OC||=sqrt3) into one math span via
  \sqrt{2}\,\text{and}\,\|...; split into two math spans with plain-text
  "and" between them, matching the skill's guidance against \text{and}
  joins.

- Disco-ball gravity exercise: $\|\text{g}\|=9.8$ $\text{N/kg}$ split the
  quantity and its unit into two adjacent math spans; joined into one
  quantity $\|\text{g}\|=9.8\,\text{N/kg}$, consistent with this file's
  other quantity+unit spans (e.g. $50\,\text{N}$).

- Suspended-block figure description: the accessibility label for point S
  read "-2squareroots of 3", the only sibling label using the plural
  "squareroots" instead of "squareroot" used by every other point label in
  the same figure (P, R, Q); corrected to "squareroot" for consistency.
  Also corrected "30 k g" to "30 kg" in the same figure description (the
  mass label's unit had been split by a stray space).

- Final exercise (r(t)=<t,2t^2,4t^2>, techrequired): the exercise's own
  domain is declared as $t\in[0,10]$, but part (b) asked to visualize the
  path over $t\in[0,60]$, contradicting that stated domain (unlike the
  preceding analogous exercise, which restates the same domain in both the
  setup and part (b)). Corrected part (b) to $t\in[0,10]$ to match the
  domain given for r(t) itself.

